        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Checksum offload flags no longer force a long BD; offload silently dropped",
        "explanation": "Packets that request only TCP, UDP or IP checksum offload no longer make bnxt_xmit_need_long_bd() return true. They are sent with a short BD. Only the long BD carries the lflags that enable L3/L4 checksum insertion. Such packets go out with no checksum computed, which corrupts traffic for the common case of plain checksum offload.",
        "suggestion": "Restore RTE_MBUF_F_TX_TCP_CKSUM, RTE_MBUF_F_TX_UDP_CKSUM and RTE_MBUF_F_TX_IP_CKSUM in the mask.",
